  "statement": "Find the area of the triangle with vertices $(1,2)$, $(4,6)$ and $(5,1)$.",
  "solution": "Using the shoelace formula, area $=\\tfrac12|1(6-1)+4(1-2)+5(2-6)|=\\tfrac12|5-4-20|=\\tfrac{19}{2}$.",
  "hints": [
    "Use the determinant/shoelace formula for area.",
    "Take the absolute value and halve."
